{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix rank matrix rank","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","fileName":"Matrix Rank.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Rank","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matrix and Vector Computation]] · [[Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Row Echelon Form","Coefficient Matrix","Augmented Matrix","Linear System","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix rank matrix rank","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","fileName":"Matrix Rank.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Rank","heading":"Matrix Rank","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The rank of a matrix is the number of linearly independent rows, which equals the number of linearly independent columns. It can be read as the number of pivots in a [[Row Echelon Form]].\n\nRank determines how much independent information a matrix contains. A square matrix has an inverse exactly when it has full rank, while rank comparisons of a [[Coefficient Matrix]] and its [[Augmented Matrix]] help determine whether a [[Linear System]] is consistent.\n\nIn a design matrix, rank counts the independently estimable columns. If rank is smaller than the number of model terms, the least-squares coefficients are not unique and at least one intended scientific effect cannot be separated from the others.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Row Echelon Form","Coefficient Matrix","Augmented Matrix","Linear System","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix rank matrix rank","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Rank.md","fileName":"Matrix Rank.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Rank","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Row Echelon Form","Coefficient Matrix","Augmented Matrix","Linear System","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}